# Cursor AI Rules for mac-pdfium Project

## Markdown File Formatting
- When generating or editing any Markdown (.md) files, ensure the file ends with EXACTLY ONE newline character (\n)
- NEVER use multiple consecutive newlines (\n\n or more) at the end of files
- This is critical for MD extension compatibility
- Applies to all .md and .markdown files

## File Ending Standard
- All text files should end with a single newline character (POSIX standard)
- Use `\n` not `\n\n` when writing file contents

